# What `docker build` may see from the repository (deploy/images/*.Dockerfile build from the root).
# Without this every build sent local caches, test suites and the git-ignored .env to the builder,
# and the nexovue image carried 37 MB of a mypy cache (docs/changes/ready-to-deploy, T4).

# Secrets and local state — never sent, let alone copied.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
.backups
.claude
CLAUDE.local.md
.playwright-mcp

# History, environments and caches the images rebuild themselves.
.git
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/dist

# Tests and development tools are not part of a release.
apps/*/tests
packages/*/tests
tools
**/*_test.go

# Documents, except the setup pages the console build turns into routes.
docs
!docs/product/setup
